{"title":"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are on a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8e7d324ea465aef56f3f3e708d966da9db8e90e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=6$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Midpoint\" title=\"Midpoint\">midpoint</a> of the minor arc <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. What is the length of the line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/e/c0e28752d93e4394719fd81fa0a030a81f7d3f3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ \\sqrt{10}\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\frac{7}{2}\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ \\sqrt{14}\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ \\sqrt{15}\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"419\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the center of the circle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/0019a9c6ae9bef5eda9166daa34ea37465190dd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{OC}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> (then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />). <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/6/bd6f8e841ed27ce2071718832e98b6d1e38c4d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA=OB=5$\" width=\"114\" height=\"13\" />, since they are both radii of the circle.\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd3aa670574ebe99dcdc49faa66af5ec3c509a15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD = \\sqrt{OA^2 - DA^2} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />, and by subtraction, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f779926ba104b640634edc11457011f8bba9cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=OC - OD = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"167\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Using the Pythagorean Theorem again, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e23643ee15cf0d5dd521a08a185cad79958435bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC= \\sqrt{AD^2 + CD^2} = \\sqrt{3^2+1^2}=\\sqrt{10} \\Longrightarrow \\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"383\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/1693c6eeb9fc858edd2c8234bff0187a61d258bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pen d = linewidth(0.8); pathpen = d; pointpen = black; pen f = fontsize(9); path p = CR((0,0),5); pair O = (0,0), A=(5,0), B = IP(p,CR(A,6)), C = IP(p,CR(A,3)), D=IP(A--B,O--C); D(p); D(MP(&quot;A&quot;,A,E)--D(MP(&quot;O&quot;,O))--MP(&quot;B&quot;,B,NE)--cycle); D(A--MP(&quot;C&quot;,C,ENE),dashed+d); D(O--C,dashed+d); D(rightanglemark(O,D(MP(&quot;D&quot;,D,W)),A)); MP(&quot;5&quot;,(A+O)/2); MP(&quot;3&quot;,(A+D)/2,SW); [/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"652\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B\">2008 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a>